What is it?
-----------

RoT_UseWall is what I and my co-creator, Lord Darkside, refer to as an
usenet/internet wall.  The idea is that multiple BBSes (all supporting
usenet/internet email) "share" one large wall - so, that if a user on
board A posts something to their wall, it also (eventually :)) shows
up on all the other boards running the wall.


Requirements
------------

- UUCP software (this version was written specifically for Matt Dillon's
  UUCP v1.16 -- not having any other packages available I have no idea
  whatsoever if this will work with other UUCP software).  Let me know
  what you need and I'll add it.
- Other BBSes to connect to (you are welcome to add me to your list).


Installation
------------

1) Assign the logical handle "RoT_DATA:" to Excelsior!' DATA directory.
   (this is needed for the importer - for convienience)
2) Copy the file `Rot_UseWall.cfg' to Excelsior!'s DATA directory and
   modify it (instructions for the various options is included in the
   file).  THIS IS VERY IMPORTANT!
3) Add the following line to your UULIB:aliases file:
		wall: "|<path>/WallImporter"
	where <path> is the path of where you store the WallImporter program
   (included in the archive).
   What this does is everytime you receive mail for the user "wall", instead
   of saving it to your UUMAIL: directory, instead it is passed to the
   WallImporter program.  It then incorporates the new entry into the
   wall.
4) Find someplace to add the RoT_UseWall program to your BBS.
   I added mine to my EX.BBSMenus file as follows:
     50,   W,        0,      "1-32",           "\#3exdev:wall/rot_usewall\"
     50,   WALL,     0,      "1-32",           "\#3exdev:wall/rot_usewall\"

You are done.  Now all you need is to locate other sites to share the wall
with.  Feel free to drop me a line if you wish to join our little network
up here in Canada :-)

To recap:  Any mail that now arrives for "wall@<your site>" will be
incorporated into your wall.  Make certain that ONLY mail from other
RoT_UseWall programs is sent to you at this address... I prefer not to
be around when some regular email gets imported into your wall *grin*

*** NOTE : For this current version of the wall, PLEASE set the EXCLUSIVE
           (ie. only one user at a time) flag!  For the next release I'll
           add in semaphores to deal with this.

Maintenance
-----------

Is performed automagically by RoT_UseWall.  Whenever it is started, it
will read-in the wall data and discard any entries that are expired (see
the RoT_UseWall.cfg file for setting the expiry date on entries).


